🔌 Hardware Requirements
ESP32 Dev Module

INA219 current/voltage sensor

SSD1306 OLED (I²C)

Limit switches (open/close detection)

Motor driver (L298N, BTS7960, or similar)

12V battery or solar system

Temperature sensor (e.g., DS18B20 or analog sensor)

⚙️ Setup Instructions
1. Clone the repo
bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/PoultryPortal.git
cd PoultryPortal
2. Install PlatformIO
https://platformio.org/install

3. Configure WiFi + Telegram
Edit your configuration via the Telegram bot or by modifying defaults in Config.cpp.

4. Build & Upload
bash
pio run --target upload
5. OTA Updates
Once running:

bash
pio run --target upload --upload-port <device-ip>
📲 Telegram Commands
Command	Description
/open	Open the door
/close	Close the door
/status	Full system status
/health	Battery + temperature health
/auto	Enable/disable auto mode
/offsets	Set sunrise/sunset offsets
/debug	Debug tools
🧠 Architecture Overview
The firmware is built around clean separation of concerns:

main.cpp → High‑level orchestration only

AutoMode → Sunrise/sunset logic

Scheduler → Solar calculations

Motor → Door movement + safety

Battery → Voltage/current + alerts

Energy → Daily mAh tracking

Display → OLED UI

TelegramRouter → Command routing

TimeUtils → NTP + timezone + uptime

WiFiSetup → WiFiManager wrapper

SystemStatus → Health snapshots

Logging → Persistent logs

Config → Preferences storage

This makes the system robust, testable, and easy to extend.

🐛 Debugging
Enable debug mode via Telegram:

Code
/debug
Or view logs on the OLED or serial monitor.